# Source artwork archives and originals.
# The processed WebP images under server/uploads/ are what the app serves and
# are tracked; these multi-megabyte originals are inputs, not deliverables.
*.zip
DrChemistar product image.jpg/
11 DrChemistar product imagejpg/

# OCR working files (Tesseract language data + cached OCR output)
*.traineddata
server/scratch/

# Source certificate archives and scans - reference material, not deliverables.
# ~50 MB of binaries that git would carry in every clone forever.
*.7z
CIR CERTIFICATE - DR CHEMISTAR CROP CARE/

# Local data stores and API response dumps.
# server/data/farmers.json is the JSON fallback for real farmer registrations,
# and list.json was a saved GET /api/farmers response - both hold personal data
# that must never reach the repository.
server/data/farmers.json
server/data/farmer-audit-log.json
server/list.json

# Transient extraction workspace used by the ZIP importer.
# public/uploads/ itself IS tracked - it is the deployed product artwork.
public/uploads/temp/
